course: dictionary
lesson: 6211
title: A misstatement is a wrong statement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A statement is something said or written as a fact. A misstatement is a statement that is wrong or not exact. Look at the parts of the word: mis- means wrong, as in mistake, and statement is the thing said.
explain: Often a misstatement is an accident, not a trick. In official reports, it can mean a false figure or claim. «The report had a misstatement of the total cost.» The word is careful and formal: it names a wrong fact in a serious document.
explain: The example «A misstatement is an official word for a lie or false claim» is only partly right. A lie is always deliberate, but a misstatement can be an honest mistake. So a misstatement is wrong, but it does not always mean someone meant to deceive.
explain: Check with context. Ask whether the sentence is about a simple mistake or a false claim in an official report. If you can swap in "wrong fact" and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A misstatement is a statement that is wrong or not exact.
fact: A misstatement is often made by accident.
fact: In official reports, a misstatement is a false figure or claim.
fact: «Correct a misstatement» means to put a wrong fact right.
fact: «A misstatement of the facts» means the facts were told wrongly.
exercise: What is a misstatement? | *A statement that is wrong or not exact | A question asked politely | A list of things to buy at the shop
exercise: «The report had a misstatement of the total cost.» What does misstatement mean here? | A long walk to the shop | *A wrong figure in an official report | A map of the city | A cheerful song about money
exercise: What does «correct a misstatement» mean? | To hide a fact from everyone | To repeat a wrong fact again and again | *To put a wrong fact right | To read a story out loud
test: «The newspaper printed a misstatement about the football score.» What does misstatement mean here? | A kind of football boot | A poem about football | A correct score that was praised by fans | *A wrong statement, often by accident
test: Which plain English phrase best matches misstatement? | A quiet noise | *A wrong fact | A happy story | A large meal
exam: Which sentence uses misstatement correctly? | The dog ate a misstatement for lunch | The sun was a misstatement at noon | *The team made a misstatement of the facts when it reported the wrong result by mistake | She sang a misstatement during the school play
